00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:35.460
packin an UM-brella and parcels cruisin through some snowy woods.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:40.000
And on the real, C.S. Lewis actually pulled a Professor Kirke

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.740
livin’ in the country during the war and
givin’ evacuees a place to crash.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:51.640
Apparently, one of the kids stayin with him was always askin Lewis bout his wardrobe, so...

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:56.860
But dis book ain’t just bout saving children, but saving them - straight Jesus style.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:07:00.800
Cuz you know C.S. Lewis like to keep it church.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:06.680
All da backward-ass sh*t dat Edmund do in da book reppin da ways dat humanity can be tempted into a life of sin;

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:13.000
and dat even though the man upstairs gonna forgive you, you might have to beast through some gnarly sh*t to get there.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.300
The cross ain’t light, naw what I mean?

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:19.740
Jus’ look at Edmund: after the white witch
promise him a life of sittin high baller on da throne

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:25.960
grubbin on dank sweets all day erry day, brutha ready to backstab his own fam like it don't even matter.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:30.060
Thing is, Edmund don’t
even get close to livin dat high life.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:37.960
What C.S. preachin here is dat a life of sin may seem like it gonna give you da life of yo dreams, but truth is, it never do.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:44.200
There’s only one hustla dat can give you
legit joy in life - Aslan, da nappy Jesus lion.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:49.000
Jus peep these similarities between dat puss and the big J.C., son:

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:53.660
Aslan sacrifices himself to save someone else, he gets hated on right befo his death:

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.860
Plus,he gets resurrected, and wit dat resurrection, lays down a new code -

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:19.060
a divine code that makes magic look like it ain't sh*t.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:24.720
Lion Jesus even use his breath to turn the White Witch’s statues back in to living creatures,

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.960
which is an analogy dat Lewis actually use in his book "Mere Christianity."

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:44.940
And if all dis holy rollin ain’t obvious enough, Lewis say in “Voyage of the Dawn Treader” that

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:50.740
Aslan got a different name in our world - someone who arrived in our world the same time as Santa Claus,

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:56.280
was the son of an Emperor, was merced for someone else’s fault, came back to life,

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.300
and is sometimes referred to as a lamb.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:02.240
Hm. I wonder who he talkin 'bout.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:07.420
But look, jus cuz we got a bunch of similarities like these don’t mean we dealin with a straight-up allegory.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.100
There are some pretty important differences.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:14.520
For one, Jesus died for EVERYONE in da hood, where as Aslan died just for Edmund.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:17.200
As Lewis say, the Chronicles are “supposal.”

00:09:17.207 --> 00:09:23.760
What he meant by that is this: suppose that the Christian God had created a whole different world dat needed rescuin?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:28.020
How might he go bout savin dat world like he saved ours?

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:35.460
Truth is, what really matters is the message: There’s a right path to go down, but fo some reason, we don’t always take it.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:41.020
Homies gonna trip, and we gonna need the love and sacrifice of somebody else so we can get back to rollin righteous.

